      "source": [
        "### Questions\n",
        "- What information do you get from `ollama list` vs `ollama ps`?\n",
        "- What is the difference between a model that is **downloaded** and one that is **loaded**?\n",
        "\n",
        "**✍️ Answer:**\n",
        "\n",
        "- **`ollama list`** (API `/api/tags`) shows the models **stored on disk**: name and tag, ID (digest), size on disk and last modification date. Through the API you also get the family, number of parameters and quantization level.\n",
        "- **`ollama ps`** (API `/api/ps`) shows the models **currently loaded in memory**: name, memory used, where it runs (`PROCESSOR`, e.g. `100% GPU` or `48%/52% CPU/GPU`), context size and `UNTIL` — when it will be unloaded.\n",
        "- A **downloaded** model is just a set of weight files on disk (in `~/.ollama/models`). It uses disk space but no RAM and cannot answer yet.\n",
        "- A **loaded** model has its weights copied into RAM/VRAM and is ready to answer immediately. The first request after a pause pays a loading time (`load_duration`). Ollama keeps a model loaded for 5 minutes after the last request (`keep_alive`), then frees the memory. So `list` is about storage, and `ps` is about memory and active use."
      ]
    },
