      "source": [
        "### Question\n",
        "Why does the model remember the name? Is the LLM itself remembering?\n",
        "\n",
        "**✍️ Answer:**\n",
        "\n",
        "The model \"remembers\" the name only because **the application re-sends the whole conversation in every request**. The `history` list stores each `User:` / `Assistant:` turn, and the printed prompt above shows that the second call contained \"My name is Ahmed.\" before \"What is my name?\". The model simply reads the answer in its prompt.\n",
        "\n",
        "**The LLM itself does not remember anything.** It is stateless: nothing is stored in the model between calls, and its weights don't change during inference. The same question sent without history (the last line of the test) gets no correct name. The \"memory\" lives in the application and is limited by the model's **context window**. Because the prompt grows with every turn, long conversations become slower, and eventually old turns must be truncated or summarised (the final app keeps the last 6 exchanges).\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "#### Better approach: the `/api/chat` endpoint\n",
        "Ollama also has a chat endpoint taking structured `messages` (with `system` / `user` / `assistant` roles) and applying the model's own chat template."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "c054",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c054",
        "outputId": "26d020db-41b1-4374-c472-c2e3b225e77a"
      },
      "source": [
        "def chat(messages, model=None, **kw):\n",
        "    payload = {\"model\": model or MODEL, \"messages\": messages, \"stream\": False, \"think\": False, **kw}\n",
        "    return post_ollama(\"/api/chat\", payload)\n",
        "\n",
        "msgs = [{\"role\": \"system\", \"content\": \"You are a concise assistant.\"},\n",
        "        {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"My name is Ahmed.\"}]\n",
        "reply = chat(msgs)[\"message\"]\n",
        "msgs.append({\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": reply[\"content\"]})\n",
        "msgs.append({\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"What is my name?\"})\n",
        "print(chat(msgs)[\"message\"][\"content\"])"
      ],
      "execution_count": 30,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Your name is Ahmed.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
