    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "c069",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c069",
        "outputId": "918b5220-df0f-4e9a-eb4d-f45b6ca1dd31"
      },
      "source": [
        "def ask_document(question, document):\n",
        "    prompt = f\"\"\"\n",
        "Answer the question using only the following document.\n",
        "\n",
        "DOCUMENT:\n",
        "{document}\n",
        "\n",
        "QUESTION:\n",
        "{question}\n",
        "\n",
        "If the answer is not contained in the document,\n",
        "say: \"Information not available.\"\n",
        "\"\"\"\n",
        "    return ask(prompt, think=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "a1 = ask_document(\"What is reinforcement learning?\", document)\n",
        "print(a1, \"\\n\")\n",
        "# Ask the out-of-document question 3 times to check consistency\n",
        "a2 = [ask_document(\"What is quantum computing?\", document) for _ in range(3)]\n",
        "for a in a2:\n",
        "    print(\"->\", a.strip()[:200])\n",
        "grounded = sum(\"not available\" in a.lower() for a in a2)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nInstruction respected {grounded}/3 times for the out-of-document question.\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 38,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "[0.5s]\n",
            "Reinforcement learning learns through interaction with an environment using rewards and penalties. \n",
            "\n",
            "[0.2s]\n",
            "[0.2s]\n",
            "[0.2s]\n",
            "-> Information not available.\n",
            "-> Information not available.\n",
            "-> Information not available.\n",
            "\n",
            "Instruction respected 3/3 times for the out-of-document question.\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c070",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c070"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Observe:** the second answer should be *\"Information not available.\"* — the model is grounded in the supplied document instead of its own training data.\n",
        "\n",
        "**✍️ Observation:** for \"What is reinforcement learning?\" the model answers from the document: learning through interaction with an environment using rewards and penalties. For \"What is quantum computing?\" the counter above shows how often it respected the instruction and answered \"Information not available.\". Small models usually do, but not always. Sometimes they add an explanation from their own training knowledge, or paraphrase the refusal sentence. This shows that **a prompt instruction is not a guarantee**. Grounding is improved by a clear system prompt, placing the instruction after the document, low temperature, and checking the answer in code."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c071",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c071"
      },
      "source": [
        "## Part 13 — Mini-RAG\n",
        "We create four documents, then build a **local retriever** that picks the most relevant one for a question and feeds it to the LLM."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "c072",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c072",
        "outputId": "18616d40-d020-4945-c95b-c01f0c3128ef"
      },
      "source": [
        "docs = {\n",
        "\"ai.txt\": \"\"\"Artificial intelligence (AI) is the field of computer science that builds systems able to perform tasks normally requiring human intelligence, such as reasoning, perception, language understanding and decision making. AI includes machine learning, expert systems, robotics and natural language processing.\"\"\",\n",
        "\n",
        "\"machine_learning.txt\": \"\"\"Machine learning is a branch of artificial intelligence. Supervised learning uses labelled data to learn a mapping from inputs to outputs (classification, regression). Unsupervised learning works with unlabelled data to discover structure such as clusters. Overfitting happens when a model memorises training data and generalises poorly.\"\"\",\n",
        "\n",
        "\"reinforcement_learning.txt\": \"\"\"Reinforcement learning learns through interaction with an environment using rewards and penalties. An agent observes a state, chooses an action, and receives a reward. The goal is to learn a policy that maximises the cumulative reward. Q-learning and policy gradients are common algorithms.\"\"\",\n",
        "\n",
        "\"deep_learning.txt\": \"\"\"Deep learning uses artificial neural networks with many layers to learn representations from large amounts of data. Convolutional neural networks are used for images, recurrent networks and transformers for sequences and language. Training deep networks usually requires GPUs.\"\"\",\n",
        "}\n",
        "\n",
        "for name, text in docs.items():\n",
        "    with open(f\"documents/{name}\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "        f.write(text)\n",
        "sorted(os.listdir(\"documents\"))"
      ],
      "execution_count": 39,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": [
              "['ai.txt',\n",
              " 'course.txt',\n",
              " 'deep_learning.txt',\n",
              " 'machine_learning.txt',\n",
              " 'reinforcement_learning.txt']"
            ]
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 39
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "c073",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c073",
        "outputId": "91bc527f-dd03-4586-fcb0-d3c261204e7f"
      },
      "source": [
        "%%writefile rag.py\n",
        "\"\"\"Mini-RAG: a tiny local retriever + prompt builder (keyword TF-IDF, no extra libraries).\"\"\"\n",
        "import math, os, re\n",
        "from collections import Counter\n",
        "\n",
        "STOPWORDS = set(\"\"\"a an the of to in on and or is are was were be by for with as at from that this\n",
        "it its what which who how why when where do does did can could should would about into using use\n",
        "learn learns through between such\"\"\".split())\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def tokenize(text):\n",
        "    return [w for w in re.findall(r\"[a-zA-Z]+\", text.lower()) if w not in STOPWORDS]\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def load_documents(folder=\"documents\"):\n",
        "    docs = {}\n",
        "    for fn in sorted(os.listdir(folder)):\n",
        "        if fn.endswith(\".txt\"):\n",
        "            with open(os.path.join(folder, fn), encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n",
        "                docs[fn] = f.read()\n",
        "    return docs\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "class Retriever:\n",
        "    def __init__(self, docs):\n",
        "        self.docs = docs\n",
        "        self.tokens = {n: Counter(tokenize(t)) for n, t in docs.items()}\n",
        "        df = Counter(w for c in self.tokens.values() for w in c)\n",
        "        N = len(docs)\n",
        "        self.idf = {w: math.log((N + 1) / (d + 0.5)) for w, d in df.items()}\n",
        "\n",
        "    def score(self, question):\n",
        "        q = tokenize(question)\n",
        "        return {\n",
        "            name: sum(self.idf.get(w, 0) * (1 + math.log(c[w])) for w in set(q) if c[w] > 0)\n",
        "            for name, c in self.tokens.items()\n",
        "        }\n",
        "\n",
        "    def top(self, question, k=1, min_score=0.01):\n",
        "        ranked = sorted(self.score(question).items(), key=lambda x: -x[1])\n",
        "        return [(n, s) for n, s in ranked[:k] if s >= min_score]\n",
        "\n",
        "    def context(self, question, k=1):\n",
        "        hits = self.top(question, k)\n",
        "        return hits, \"\\n\\n\".join(f\"[{n}]\\n{self.docs[n]}\" for n, _ in hits)\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "def build_prompt(question, context):\n",
        "    return f\"\"\"Answer the question using only the CONTEXT below.\n",
        "If the answer is not contained in the context, say: \"Information not available.\"\n",
        "\n",
        "CONTEXT:\n",
        "{context if context else '(no relevant document found)'}\n",
        "\n",
        "QUESTION:\n",
        "{question}\n",
        "\"\"\""
      ],
      "execution_count": 40,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Writing rag.py\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "c074",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c074",
        "outputId": "4d7f054b-6b64-41ae-ce21-ef33648b5a8e"
      },
      "source": [
        "import importlib, rag\n",
        "importlib.reload(rag)\n",
        "\n",
        "retriever = rag.Retriever(rag.load_documents(\"documents\"))\n",
        "\n",
        "def rag_answer(question, k=2, model=None):   # k=2: course.txt and the specific file often both match\n",
        "    hits, ctx = retriever.context(question, k)\n",
        "    out = generate(rag.build_prompt(question, ctx), model=model, think=False)\n",
        "    return hits, out[\"response\"], out[\"wall_s\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "rag_results = []\n",
        "for q in [\"What is reinforcement learning?\",\n",
        "          \"Which hardware is needed to train neural networks with many layers?\",\n",
        "          \"What is supervised learning?\",\n",
        "          \"Who won the 2018 World Cup?\"]:\n",
        "    hits, ans, t = rag_answer(q)\n",
        "    rag_results.append({\"question\": q, \"retrieved\": \", \".join(n for n, _ in hits) or \"(none)\",\n",
        "                        \"answer\": ans.strip(), \"time_s\": round(t, 1)})\n",
        "    print(f\"Q: {q}\\n  retrieved: {hits}\\n  A: {ans.strip()}\\n  ({t:.1f}s)\\n\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 41,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Q: What is reinforcement learning?\n",
            "  retrieved: [('course.txt', 1.0831034956175303), ('reinforcement_learning.txt', 1.0227918049805298)]\n",
            "  A: Reinforcement learning learns through interaction with an environment using rewards and penalties. An agent observes a state, chooses an action, and receives a reward. The goal is to learn a policy that maximises the cumulative reward. Q-learning and policy gradients are common algorithms.\n",
            "  (1.4s)\n",
            "\n",
            "Q: Which hardware is needed to train neural networks with many layers?\n",
            "  retrieved: [('deep_learning.txt', 8.42789552798877)]\n",
            "  A: According to the context, training deep networks (which are described as having many layers) usually requires **GPUs**.\n",
            "  (0.7s)\n",
            "\n",
            "Q: What is supervised learning?\n",
            "  retrieved: [('course.txt', 1.0831034956175303), ('machine_learning.txt', 1.0580718823582704)]\n",
            "  A: Supervised learning uses labelled data to learn a mapping from inputs to outputs (classification, regression).\n",
            "  (0.7s)\n",
            "\n",
            "Q: Who won the 2018 World Cup?\n",
            "  retrieved: []\n",
            "  A: Information not available.\n",
            "  (0.3s)\n",
            "\n"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "c075",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "c075"
      },
      "source": [
        "**Architecture**\n",
        "```\n",
        "Documents → Local Retriever → Relevant Context → Ollama → Local LLM → Answer\n",
        "```\n",
        "This is the fundamental idea behind **Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG)**.\n",
        "\n",
        "**✍️ Observation:** each course question retrieves the documents that share its keywords (for example `reinforcement_learning.txt` and `course.txt` for reinforcement learning, `deep_learning.txt` for the hardware question), and the model answers from them, e.g. \"training deep networks usually requires GPUs\". We keep the 2 best documents (`k=2`) because `course.txt` overlaps with the specific files and can otherwise hide the more detailed one. For \"Who won the 2018 World Cup?\" no document matches, so the context is empty and the model should answer \"Information not available.\" — even though it probably knows the answer (France). RAG lets the model use **private, up-to-date documents** it was never trained on, and limits hallucinations to what is in the context.\n",
        "\n",
        "#### Optional extension — semantic retrieval with embeddings\n",
        "Keyword matching fails when the question uses different words than the document. Ollama can also compute embeddings locally with `nomic-embed-text` (≈ 270 MB)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "c076",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        },
        "id": "c076",
        "outputId": "16a09922-5c81-419f-ce5b-e227a6a91300"
      },
      "source": [
        "EMBED_MODEL = \"nomic-embed-text\"\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "\n",
        "def embed(texts):\n",
        "    return np.array(post_ollama(\"/api/embed\", {\"model\": EMBED_MODEL, \"input\": texts})[\"embeddings\"])\n",
        "\n",
        "def semantic_top(question, docs, k=1):\n",
        "    names = list(docs)\n",
        "    D = embed([docs[n] for n in names]); q = embed([question])[0]\n",
        "    sims = D @ q / (np.linalg.norm(D, axis=1) * np.linalg.norm(q))\n",
        "    return sorted(zip(names, sims), key=lambda x: -x[1])[:k]\n",
        "\n",
        "try:\n",
        "    pull_model(EMBED_MODEL)\n",
        "    question = \"What hardware accelerates network training?\"\n",
        "    print(\"Keyword retriever :\", retriever.top(question, k=2))\n",
        "    print(\"Semantic retriever:\", [(n, round(float(s), 3)) for n, s in semantic_top(question, rag.load_documents(\"documents\"), k=2)])\n",
        "except Exception as e:\n",
        "    print(\"Optional part skipped:\", e)"
      ],
      "execution_count": 42,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
